-Use the provided spreadsheet tools to complete the requested workbook. Preserve source inputs.
+Spreadsheet task guidance.
+
+A. INSPECT API. Call workbook_inspect on the source. It returns every occupied cell with its stored value/formula, comment, computed value and column width, the used range and each column's dominant type (numeric / text). Read all comments, note the header row, and note intentional blanks.
+
+B. LAYOUT & PERIOD ALIGNMENT. Map header columns to output columns. If a value lives in a column whose header year precedes the first forecast year (a "historical" / "opening" / "pre-period" input), that column anchors the forecast and is NOT itself a forecast period: forecast growth applies to the NEXT column. Comments such as "precedes the first displayed forecast year" confirm this. When in doubt, check whether a cell in the anchoring column already holds a value; if yes it is an input, not a forecast output.
+
+C. SCENARIO SELECTION. If base-case rows and requested/selected-case rows coexist (base growth vs requested case growth, base margin vs requested case margin), forecast outputs use the REQUESTED case only. Only fall back to the base rows when no requested-case row exists.
+
+D. FORMULAS ONLY. Every computed output cell must be an Excel formula referencing in-workbook input cells. Typed constants count as wrong because the workbook is recalculated independently. Use a consistent relative-reference pattern across periods and check the first cell of each row before mirroring.
+
+E. COVERAGE. The task enumerates sections: fill every enumerated output row across every period the task asks for, and leave the cells the task calls intentionally blank untouched. If the task names a final-year-only value, compute it only there.
+
+F. VERIFY. Call workbook_audit on the delivered file. It reports: which cells hold formulas, whether each has a computed value or an error, every enumerated formula range, formula errors, and a diff versus the source confirming original inputs, labels, units, comments and intentional blanks are preserved. Fix any formula error, any requested output that is still empty, and any unintended change to source inputs, writing a fresh copy before completing. Deliver to the exact path the task requests (commonly /workspace/result.xlsx).
